hadiths[86]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3566","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A girl's father married her, she did not like (this relationship), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave her the option (to keep or annul the marriage). A narrator named Abu Khorasan narrated that a girl came to the Prophet's service and mentioned that her father had married her without her permission, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the couple. The same hadith is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Ikrima with reference to another chain of transmission, while other narrators have quoted it as a transmission from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding Ikrimah, and it is correct that it is a transmission."
"3567","Abu Salama narrates: A man from Banu Mundhir married his daughter, the girl did not like (that relationship), she came to the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the Prophet (peace be upon him) annulled her marriage."
"3568","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3569","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: A man married his daughter. The girl did not like the relationship, so the Prophet (PBUH) separated them."
"3570","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: A man married his virgin daughter. The girl did not like the relationship. She came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet declared the marriage invalid. This hadith is not proven on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayb, on the authority of Nafi, but it is correct that it is on the authority of Umar Ibn Husayn on the authority of Ibn Abi Zayb, as has already been said."
"3571","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: A man came to the Prophet (PBUH) with his daughter, and said, \My daughter is refusing to marry.\"" What is the husband's right over his wife? If there is an abscess in the husband's nose from which pus and material is coming out"
"3572","Sumak bin Harb narrates: A person came to the service of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and said: There is a girl, I am her guardian, she has married without my permission, then Sayyidna Ali (RA) said: Our opinion about what this girl has done is that if she has married me, we will uphold her, and if she has married someone who is not her kafou, then we (have the authority to uphold her). or cancel option) will give you."
"3573","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A virgin girl should not be married until her permission is obtained, and Saiba has authority over her own person, unless she invites resentment. Ishaq says: I inquired from Jesus: Is the last part of the tradition transmitted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He replied, \No"
"3574","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A female (widow or divorced woman) should not be married until her will is known, and a virgin should not be married until the adhan is taken from her and her adhan is silent."
"3575","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said: The Saiba (widow or divorced woman) is more entitled to her affairs, and permission will be taken from a virgin girl, her permission is her silence. Muammar has narrated something different from both of them in his chain of transmission, he has omitted the mention of a person from the chain of transmission, similarly, Mu'mar has narrated something different from both of them in the text of this hadith and has quoted the tradition in other words, but he has been deceived in this, because every narrator who has narrated it with reference to Abdullah bin Fazl and every narrator who has narrated it with Abdullah bin Fazl from Nafi bin Jubeer, all of them have narrated a different tradition from Muammar. And the agreement of all these narrators to narrate different narrations from Muammar is proof that Muammar is delusional about this and Allah knows best."
"3576","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A virtuous woman has more rights over her own self than her husband, and permission will be taken from a virgin girl regarding her own self, and her permission will be silent."
"3577","Abdullah bin Raja narrated the same tradition (the above-mentioned hadith) through his chain of transmission."
"3578","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The guardian has no authority over the daughter-in-law, and her will will be known from the virgin, and her silence will be her confession."
"3579","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The guardian has no authority over the daughter-in-law"
"3580","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A virgin girl will be asked about her will, and her silence will be regarded as her consent. Abu Dawud Tayalasi has narrated it in the same way with his authority."
"3581","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virtuous woman has more rights about herself than her guardian, and the will of a virgin girl will be known, and her silence will be permitted."
"3582","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A virtuous woman has more rights over herself than her guardian, and her father will find out her will (about her) from a virgin girl. A narrator named Amr has quoted these words: His permission will be his silence."
"3583","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, all its narrators have copied the word, al-Thayb."
"3584","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “A virtuous woman has more rights about herself than her guardian, and her will will be known from a virgin girl, and if she remains silent, it will be considered her consent.”"
"3585","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, “A beautiful woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and her will will be known from a virgin girl, and her permission will be her silence.” Shaykh says: There is a possibility that the word virgin girl used in this hadith refers to a virgin orphan girl. Well, Allah knows best. The reason for this is that we have mentioned this in other narrations narrated by Salih bin Qaisan and after him. Ibn Uyynah quoted these words in reference to Ziyad bin Saad: Her father will take permission from a virgin girl, so according to our knowledge, no narrator has mentioned Ibn Uyynah about these words. It may be that he mentioned this hadith based on his memory and his language was wrong, Allah knows best. The same tradition has been narrated from Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding Abu Barda, that the will of an orphan girl will be ascertained."
"3586","Sayyidina Abu Musa al-Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \The will of the orphan girl will be ascertained about her self. If she remains silent"
"3587","Abu Burdah narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said, \The will of an orphan girl will be ascertained; if she remains silent"
"3588","Abu Barda narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: The will of an orphan girl will be ascertained about her self, and her permission will be her silence."
"3589","Abu Burdah, on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that an orphan girl will be asked about her will, and if she agrees, she will be married, and if she does not agree, then she will not be married."
"3590","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A female (widow or divorced woman) has more ownership (rights) of her affairs than her guardian, and permission will be sought from a virgin girl regarding her status, and her silence will be her confession."
"3591","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to come and marry a woman in return for a souvenir."
"3592","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: We asked the Prophet (PBUH) about the dowry of women, and he (PBUH) said that its amount will be whatever the people decide between themselves."
"3593","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man marries a woman with a handful of grains (the condition of dowry), then this will be dowry. Nishapuri has quoted this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) in his hadith with reference to Muhammad bin Muslim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man gives two fistfuls of grain (as dowry) to a woman, then that woman will become halal for that person, (that is, that grain will be accepted as dowry in marriage)."
"3594","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: We used to get married in exchange for a handful of grain during the time of the Holy Prophet (PBUH)."
"3595","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Whoever fills both fists in marriage has made the marriage lawful.\"" The narrator explains: Here are probably the words for flour"
"3596","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that when a person makes a witness, there will be no harm to him, whether he marries for a small amount of wealth (as dowry) or for a large amount of wealth."
"3597","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “There is no sin on a man when he makes a witness, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth as a dowry.”"
"3598","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sin on a man when he makes a witness, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth (as a dowry)."
"3599","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man makes a witness, it will not harm him, whether he marries for a small amount of his wealth (as a dowry) or marries for a large amount of wealth (as a dowry)."
"3600","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \Marry Thayba.\"" The Prophet"
"3601","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “Marry women only in Kufu, let them be married only by saints, and the dowry should not be less than ten dirhams."
"3602","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams."
"3603","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the mahr should not be less than ten dirhams."
"3604","Shaabi says: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams."
"3605","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The dowry should not be less than five dirhams."
"3606","It is narrated along with another chain of transmission) Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: The mahr should not be less than ten dirhams."
"3607","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates with reference to his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him): Sayyiduna Ali, may God be pleased with him, says: The dowry will be whatever the husband and wife agree on."
"3608","Urwa narrates about Sayyida Umm Habiba (may God be pleased with her): She was previously the wife of Abdullah bin Jahsh. A narrator named Abd al-Razzaq narrated this: Sayyidah Umm Habiba's first husband was Ubaidullah bin Jahsh, who was a Christian."
"3609","Urwa narrates about Sayyida Umm Habiba, may Allah be pleased with her: She was the wife of Ubaydullah bin Jahsh. Ubaydullah died in Abyssinia, so Najashi married Sayyida Umm Habiba, may God bless him and grant him peace, and paid her four thousand dirhams as a dowry on his behalf, and then, along with Sayyidana Shahrabeel bin Hasnah, may God bless him and grant him peace, she was in the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace (Madinah). Munora) sent."
"3610","Ubaidullah Ashjajai narrates: I said to Sufyan: Dawood has quoted the saying of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Sha'bi that the dowry will not be less than ten dirhams."
"3611","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa’idi (RA) narrates: We were present with the Prophet (PBUH) and a woman came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and presented herself for marriage. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired, \Do you have anything (to pay as dowry)?\"" He said"
"3612","The same tradition has been quoted with reference to some other isnads. In it, the narrator named Thauri has quoted these words: I marry you to the Qur'an that comes to you."
"3613","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A woman came to the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man stood up who was wearing a cloak, which he tied around his neck. He said, O Messenger of Allah, I will marry him. He said, O Messenger of Allah, there is no Prophet. He said to them, sit down. Then the woman came again. She said, O Messenger of Allah, state your opinion about me. The same gentleman stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ask you if you have wealth? He said, O Messenger of Allah, no, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \You sit down!\"" Then the woman came again and said"
"3614","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to a person, \You should marry this woman"
"3615","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may God be pleased with him) narrates: An Ansari married a woman during illness. The people said: This is not permissible and it (inheritance) will be counted as a third share."
"3616","Saeed bin Musayb narrates this statement of an Ansari Sahabi: I married a virgin without seeing her, (after leave) when I came to her she was pregnant. The same hadith is narrated from Safwan bin Salim with reference to another chain of transmission."
"3617","Sayyidna Basra bin Abu Basra Ghafari narrates: He married a virgin girl without seeing her, later he found that girl pregnant, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two husbands and wives."
"3618","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said, \Should I not tell you about the rented ox?\"" The people said yes. The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said"
"3619","Hubayrah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Shaybani narrated to us: Abu Maysarah Ahmad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn Maysarah narrated to us: Marwan al-Fazari narrated to us: Abu ‘Abd al-Malik al-‘Ammi narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us from ‘A’ishah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Al-‘usaylah is sexual intercourse.”"
"3620","Sayyidna Aiz bin Amr Muzni (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Islam is exalted, it cannot be defeated."
"3621","Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: I sent a marriage message to a woman, the Prophet (PBUH) asked me, have you seen her? I did not say: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look at her because in this way love will be born between the two of you. A narrator named Abu Shahab has narrated these words: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sent a marriage message to a woman. The following words are as before."
"3622","Sayyidna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to marry. He mentioned this to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go and see this woman, because as a result of this, love will develop between you two. The narrator narrates: He did so and then married that woman, after which the narrator mentions their concord. This is correct: This hadith is narrated from Bikramzni on the authority of Thabit."
"3623","Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) (after that, according to the earlier hadith)."
"3624","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A man intended to marry an Ansar woman, so the Prophet (PBUH) said: Look at her, because there is something in the eyes of the women of the Ansar."
"3625","Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the remarriage of his daughter Sayyidah Zainab (may Allah be pleased with him) with Sayyidna Abul-Aas bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him). This tradition is not proven, the narration narrated by the narrator named Hajjaj cannot be presented as proof."
"3626","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) had sent his daughter Sayyida Zainab (RA) to Sayyiduna Abul-Aas bin Rabi (RA) on the basis of her first marriage, but the Prophet (PBUH) did not allow her to marry again."
"3627","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may God be pleased with him) narrates: My sister was the wife of an Ansari. This Ansari married her on the condition of paying a garden (as dowry). There was disagreement between the two of them. They presented their case to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Give her back her garden. This divorces you.\"" Then the woman said"
"3628","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said, O Messenger of God, I am not angry with him regarding his morals or religion, but I do not like ungrateful (husband) after becoming a Muslim. He said, O Thabit, take your garden and divorce him."
"3629","Abu Zubair narrates: Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (RA) married Zainab bint Abdullah, Sayyidna Thabit gave her a garden as a dowry, she did not like him. The woman said, \Yes"
"3630","Ata narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, A man should not take from a divorced woman more than what he gave her (as dowry)."
"3631","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, obtained a divorce from her husband, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fixed her period of one and a half months."
"3632","Ikrimah narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may God be pleased with her, obtained Khula from her husband, so the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fixed her period as one period."
"3633","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, obtained Khula from him, and the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, instructed this woman to remain in Idda until one period."
"3634","Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that he instructed the wife of Sayyidna Thabit bin Qays (RA) to perform ``Idah'' until one menstrual period when she obtained divorce from (her husband)."
"3635","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
"3636","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"3637","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
"3638","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There are three things in which seriousness is considered serious, and joking is also considered serious: marriage, divorce, and conversion."
"3639","Narrated Abu Huraira: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Among the signs of the Last Day is this: Shepherds of goats will become rulers of the people, and barefoot, naked bodies, (i.e. scantily clad) hungry people will build buildings higher than each other, and the maid will give birth to her master."
"3640","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth, or intercourse with a young girl until she menstruates (i.e. she becomes an adult)."
"3641","Hasan bin Muhammad and Abdullah bin Muhammad narrate this statement of their father: Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), do you not know this? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating (the meat of) domesticated donkeys and having fun."
"3642","Ayyas bin Salamah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Salamah bin Akwa, may Allah be pleased with him): On the occasion of the Battle of Uttas, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted to have intercourse with women for three days, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"3643","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyidna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) forbade sexual intercourse with women. He said that Allah had made it lawful for the people during the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At that time, the number of women was less and then it was made forbidden for the people. Now, if a person commits this act, he will be punished."
"3644","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The laws of marriage, divorce, inheritance and inheritance have declared Mutah to be haram (the narrator is in doubt or perhaps these are the words)."
"3645","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade Mut'ah."
"3646","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: He separated the husband and wife."
"3647","Qudama says: I asked Saeed bin Musaib about the marriage of a person in the state of Ihram, and he said that separation will be done between the two husbands and wives."
"3648","Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said: A person in the state of Ihram can neither marry himself nor marry anyone."
"3649","Ikramah bin Khalid narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) about a woman with whom a person who is outside Makkah wants to marry and he is going to perform Umrah or Hajj."
"3650","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself, nor can he marry anyone, nor can he give the message of marriage."
"3651","Nafi' narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: He may have quoted this as the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
